      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224414",
      ":question/problem": "An email server manager determined that $4%$ of the emails their clients receive are spam. After introducing a new filtering feature, the manager wants to know if the proportion of spam emails her clients receive has decreased. She decides to test the following hypotheses at the $10%$ significance level.\n\n- $H_{0}: p = 0.04$\n- $H_{1}: p < 0.04$\n\nHere, $p$ is the proportion of spam emails.\n\nThe manager samples $50$ client emails and notices that only $1$ is spam.\n\nLet $X$ equal the number of spam emails in a random sample. State the distribution of $X$ under $H_{0}$, the value of $\u03b1$, and specify a suitable test statistic for this hypothesis test.\n\nThe distribution of $X$ under the null hypothesis is $X\u223c$ {{field-1}}.\n\nA suitable test statistic is $P($ {{field-2}} $)$.\n\nThe significance level is $\u03b1 =$ {{field-3}}"
    },
