      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224907",
      ":question/problem": "A customer in a casino suspects that a roulette wheel numbered from $1$ to $36$ is biased toward landing on $9$. After alerting the croupier, they inspect the wheel and decide to test the following hypotheses at the $10%$ significance level.\n\n- $H_{0}: p = \\frac{1}{36}$\n- $H_{1}: p > \\frac{1}{36}$\n\nHere, $p$ represents the probability that the roulette lands on $9$.\n\nThe croupier sampled $100$ random spins of the roulette wheel and noticed that it landed on $9$ on $5$ occasions.\n\nLet $X$ be the number of times the roulette wheel lands on $9$ in a random sample. State the distribution of $X$ under $H_{0}$, the value of $\u03b1$, and specify a suitable test statistic for this hypothesis test.\n\nThe distribution of $X$ under the null hypothesis is $X\u223c$ {{field-1}}.\n\nA suitable test statistic is $P($ {{field-2}} $)$.\n\n$\u03b1 =$ {{field-3}}"
    }
